\section{AAE and CGR Analysis}

\paragraph{Correlations between Owner and Paper Scores:}
The results of the author reviews, as shown in Table~\ref{tab:scores}, show a positive but low correlation between owner scores and paper scores. This is important because it implies that the owner's score should not be treated as the same as the paper score by the LLM. By default, their system treats owner scores and paper scores as equal for LLM CGR and AAE. They should do more to limit the influence of owner scores, especially when these scores are given by the owner of the paper. In fact, they can even choose to discard scores from the owner, if they show a high score for the paper. 
